{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## AC1 — MEASURED live counts (growth vs. widening: GROWTH, widening REFUTED)\n\nMeasured 2026-09-05 against the live REB project (`https://navasage.atlassian.net`) with\nread-only `POST /rest/api/3/search/approximate-count`. No bridge write, no mutation.\n\n| Query | 2026-05-26 baseline | 2026-09-05 measured | Delta |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `project = REB AND statusCategory != \"Done\"` (active) | 1,050 | **1,388** | +338 (+32%) |\n| `project = REB AND statusCategory = \"Done\"` (done) | 1,120 | **2,992** | +1,872 (+167%) |\n| `project = REB` (total) | 2,170 | **4,380** | +2,210 (+102%) |\n\nActive is 1,388 against a 1,200 ceiling: the active query is over by 188. That is the failing\nquery. The Done query cannot be the trigger — `_iter_pages` clips it at `_DONE_RECENT_CAP=1000`\n(the cap branch returns before cumulative could reach 1,200), so its 2,992 matches are already\nbeing reduced to the most-recent 1,000 by design.\n\n### Widening is REFUTED, three independent ways\n\n1. **Direct A/B of the old and new JQL against live data.** The only change to the query text\n   since the baseline probe was `status != \"Done\"` -> `statusCategory != \"Done\"`\n   (`3e5c7d39feaa`, 2026-08-15, ticket 7332). Both forms measured today:\n   - `project = REB AND status != \"Done\"` -> **1,388**\n   - `project = REB AND statusCategory != \"Done\"` -> **1,388**\n\n   Identical. The switch matched zero additional issues.\n2. **REB's status set makes it a no-op.** REB exposes exactly `To Do`/`IDEA` (To Do),\n   `In Progress`/`In Review`/`Blocked` (In Progress), `Done` (Done). No Closed/Resolved/Cancelled,\n   so there is nothing for `statusCategory` to reclassify. If anything the switch could only\n   *narrow* active, never widen it.\n3. **Timing.** The statusCategory change landed 2026-08-15 and was followed by three weeks of\n   green hourly runs, including the eleven immediately before the failure. `git log` shows no\n   commit touching `jql_active` / `jql_done_recent` / `_ACLI_CEILING` between the last success\n   (00:59) and the first failure (01:33) — the JQL text has been byte-identical since 08-15.\n\n**Verdict: organic growth.** The active working set grew 1,050 -> 1,388 in ~14 weeks and crossed\nthe 1,200 ceiling. Nothing widened. This confirms the ticket's framing: the ceiling is a vendor\nlimit, the working set only grows, and the defect is that reconciliation capacity is coupled to\ntotal project size.\n\n## A second finding: `issuekey`-range partitioning is a SILENT-DROP TRAP — rejected\n\nKey-range slicing (`issuekey >= REB-a AND issuekey < REB-b`) was the first partition candidate:\nkeys are dense and monotonic, so a window of width W bounds the slice at W issues regardless of\nproject size. Measured against live Jira before adopting it, and it fails exactly the way this\nticket warns about:\n\n```\nproject = REB AND statusCategory != \"Done\" AND issuekey < REB-5373   ->  1387   (REB-5373 exists)\nproject = REB AND statusCategory != \"Done\" AND issuekey < REB-5501   ->     0   (REB-5501 does NOT exist)\nproject = REB AND statusCategory != \"Done\" AND issuekey < REB-9999   ->     0   (does NOT exist)\n```\n\nA relational `issuekey` comparison whose **boundary key does not exist** matches nothing, and\nreturns **no error**. Max key is REB-5373 while `project = REB` holds 4,380 issues, so ~1,000 key\nslots are gaps (deleted/moved issues) — any window whose boundary lands in a gap silently\ncontributes zero. A naive 500-wide tiling over REB-1..REB-5500 summed to **979** against a true\n1,388: **409 issues silently lost, raising nothing.** That is this bug wearing a new hat, and it\nwould have been invisible without measuring coverage.\n\n## Chosen partition key: `created` half-open windows\n\n`created` was validated the same way — an 8-window half-open tiling summed **exactly** to the\nwhole space:\n\n```\n[1970-01-01, 2026-01-01) 0    [2026-01-01, 2026-04-01) 0    [2026-04-01, 2026-06-01) 0\n[2026-06-01, 2026-07-01) 6    [2026-07-01, 2026-08-01) 61   [2026-08-01, 2026-08-15) 20\n[2026-08-15, 2026-09-01) 446  [2026-09-01, 2030-01-01) 855\nsum = 1388   whole-space = 1388\n```\n\nTwo properties decide it over the alternatives:\n\n- **Totality does not depend on a value existing.** `created < X` / `created >= X` partition the\n  space for *any* X, real issue or not — the exact property `issuekey` lacks.\n- **`created` is immutable.** `updated` changes under a running pass, so an issue touched\n  mid-scan can migrate between windows and be missed (or double-counted). `created` never moves,\n  so the windows are stable for the whole pass.\n\nDesign and seam guarantees to follow in the implementation comment."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788573739033878578,"uuid":"c5f89acf-9935-4762-837f-938cad69b39d"}